# Manual REST Client requests for GET /people, PUT /people/:id/role, POST /people/:id/remove, GET /people/removed and POST /people/:id/restore (VS Code REST Client).
# Sign in with any approved review account of REVIEW_ACCOUNTS in apps/backend/.env: set the email and code below.
# Codes are read from the backend log when RESEND_API_KEY is unset.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@email = admin@example.com
@code = 345678

### Request a sign-in code (expects 202)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email/code
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "locale": "pt-BR"
}

### Sign in (expects 200 with accessToken)
# @name session
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "code": "{{code}}"
}

###
@token = {{session.response.body.accessToken}}

### Default list: approved users, A–Z by name (ignoring case and accents), 20 per page (expects 200 with { items: [{ id, name, role, createdAt, whatsappNumber }], page, perPage, total })
GET {{baseUrl}}/people
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filter by one or more roles (comma separated) and search the name ignoring case and accents (expects 200; "joao" finds "João")
GET {{baseUrl}}/people?role=student,instructor&search=joao
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Second page (expects 200; items: [] past the end, with the real total)
GET {{baseUrl}}/people?page=2&perPage=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Without a token (expects 401 auth.token.invalid)
GET {{baseUrl}}/people

### As a pending, denied, deleted or removed account (expects 403 user.status.notApproved): use that account's token
GET {{baseUrl}}/people
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Invalid query (expects 422 with errors people.page.invalid, people.perPage.invalid, people.role.invalid)
GET {{baseUrl}}/people?page=0&perPage=51&role=guest
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Change someone's role, as an approved admin (expects 200 { id, role }). Allowed: student → instructor or admin,
### instructor → admin or student, admin → instructor. A student gives up their upcoming seats and pending requests;
### an instructor made a student leaves their upcoming classes. The person gets a role.changed notification.
@personId = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
PUT {{baseUrl}}/people/{{personId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "instructor"
}

### Missing or unknown role (expects 422 people.role.invalid)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/people/{{personId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "guest"
}

### Refusals: a student or instructor caller (403 user.role.notAdmin); an unknown id (404 user.notFound); one's own id
### (403 user.role.self); a person who isn't approved (409 user.status.notApproved); admin → student or the same role
### (409 user.role.changeNotAllowed); a change that would leave no approved admin (409 user.role.lastAdmin)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/people/{{personId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "student"
}

### Remove someone from the platform, as an approved admin (expects 200 { id, status: "removed" }). The account gives up its
### upcoming seats, pending requests and class assignments; its sessions stay, so it signs in to see "Access removed". The
### person gets an account.removed notification.
POST {{baseUrl}}/people/{{personId}}/remove
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Refusals: a student or instructor caller (403 user.role.notAdmin); an unknown id (404 user.notFound); one's own id
### (403 user.remove.self); a person who isn't approved (409 user.status.notApproved); the only approved admin
### (409 user.role.lastAdmin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/people/{{personId}}/remove
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Removed accounts still inside their 30-day window, most recent removal first
### (expects 200 { items: [{ id, name, role, whatsappNumber, removedAt }] })
GET {{baseUrl}}/people/removed
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Restore a removed account within 30 days (expects 200 { id, status: "approved" }). It keeps its role and history; the
### seats, requests and classes the removal released stay released. The person gets an account.restored notification.
POST {{baseUrl}}/people/{{personId}}/restore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Refusals: an account that isn't removed (409 user.status.notRemoved); one removed 30 days ago or more
### (409 removal.window.ended); an unknown id (404 user.notFound)
POST {{baseUrl}}/people/{{personId}}/restore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
